// SPDX-License-Identifier: LicenseRef-Nordic-5-Clause
//
// IronSide TE two-phase provisioning, PHASE 1: Empty -> PRoT Provisioning.
// Installs the images, the rollback counters and every OTA KEK generation, then
// engages the protection registers.
//
// Step 3 of 4, referencing no files. See single_phase.jlink for the full
// sequence, for why step 2 must program the RAM sections too, for the
// must-not-boot-in-between rule, and for why the exit code is not a verdict --
// this script's device steps are identical to it.
//
//   1. erase the part                  see the production programming guide
//   2. program production_two_phase_1.hex        ALL of it -- NVM/UICR *and* RAM
//   3. JLinkExe -nogui 1 -SelectEmuBySN <SN> -CommandFile two_phase_1.jlink \
//              -Log results/two_phase_1.log
//   4. check_prov_result.py --bundle production_two_phase_1.hex --result results/result.bin
//
// The bundle comes from:
//   ironside_bundle.py build-production-hex <bundle> -o <dir>
//
// which writes this phase's hex and phase 2's alongside the single-phase hex.
// The bundle must be prepared first -- update-keys, then sign-component.
//
// One difference from the single-phase flow, and it is in the batch that bundle
// carries rather than in anything below: this one does not close the non-secure
// AP. SECAPPROTECT here takes the secure AP away at the commit reset;
// set-approtect is phase 2's whole job, and by then only the non-secure firmware
// can reach it.
//
// Emitted from Unseeded, as the single-phase bundle is, so one artifact serves a
// factory-fresh part: the batch enrolls the IKG seed and exports the IAK, and a
// part already holding a seed takes the same bundle (the enrollment tolerates its
// own failure, and the seed survives ERASEALL). A bundle emitted from Empty
// instead carries neither op -- feed a fresh part that and it reaches PRoT with no
// device identity and no usable OTA KEK, sealed and unrecoverable.

EoE 1
SelectInterface SWD
Speed 4000
Device Cortex-M33
Connect

// --- Catch the core at its reset vector, before IROT runs. Must preserve the
// --- RAM written in step 2 -- see single_phase.jlink.
Reset
WaitHalt 3000

// --- Clear the result header.
W4 0x20071000, 0x00000000
W4 0x20071004, 0x00000000
W4 0x20071008, 0x00000000
W4 0x2007100C, 0x00000000

// --- Redirect into the secure provisioning firmware.
// --- No R13 write: Commander has no spelling for register index 13, and the core
// --- resets with SPSEL=0 so R13 is the banked MSP written above -- see
// --- single_phase.jlink.
W4 0xE000ED08, 0x20013000
WReg MSP, 0x20032800
SetPC 0x20012800
WReg XPSR, 0x01000000
Go

WaitHalt 10000
SaveBin results/result.bin, 0x20071000, 0x200

// --- Commit with a pin reset. SECAPPROTECT takes effect here: after this the
// --- secure AP is gone and nothing in this script could run again.
WriteDP 2 0x02000000
WriteAP 0 0x00000004
WriteAP 0 0x00000000
qc
